<title>GERMANY: Anzag says 95/96 net profit up 19 pct.</title>
<headline>Anzag says 95/96 net profit up 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business year 1995/1996 ending August 31.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   38.5	 32.3</p>
<p>    Group sales				  4,313.2 vs 4,056.2</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    57.7    vs 49.9</p>
<p>    DVFA results per share		   40	vs 37 marks</p>
<p>    Equity/Assets ratio			42	vs 38 pct</p>
<p>    Return on Equity			   13.6    vs 11.3 pct</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    2,315   vs 2,358</p>
<p>    Dividend				     18	vs 14 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German pharmaceutical wholesaler is Andreae-Noris Zahn AG. The group said it would suggest reducing the nominal value of its shares from 50 marks to five marks this year.</p>
</text>
